"proof_check.py (lines 1-30 of 331, 11538 bytes)\n     1→\"\"\"A minimal proof checker for the equational theory of `arith.add` / `arith.multiply`.\n     2→\n     3→It verifies conjectures over the free term algebra of the integers with the\n     4→two operations `+` and `*` and the usual ring/semiring axioms, by reducing\n     5→both sides of a conjecture to a canonical multivariate-polynomial normal\n     6→form (integer coefficients, monomials sorted by total degree, then\n     7→lexicographically by exponent tuple) and comparing the normal forms.\n     8→\n     9→This is the classical AC-normalisation (\"Buchberger-free\") approach for the\n    10→theory of commutative semirings: two polynomials are provably equal from the\n    11→semiring axioms (commutativity, associativity, distributivity, identity\n    12→elements) **iff** their canonical normal forms coincide.  Soundness therefore\n    13→holds both ways: equal normal forms prove the conjecture; distinct normal\n    14→forms are a genuine counterexample witness (the semiring axioms cannot prove\n    15→them equal, and any concrete integer instantiation of the variables that\n    16→differs numerically certifies the conjecture is false over the integers).\n    17→\n    18→No third-party dependencies; only the Python standard library is used.\n    19→\n    20→Usage\n    21→-----\n    22→    python3 proof_check.py goals.py\n    23→\n    24→where `goals.py` is a Python file defining the names\n    25→`IDENTITIES`, `COMMUTATIVITY`, `ASSOCIATIVITY`, `DISTRIBUTIVITY`\n    26→(lists of conjectures) and the optional auxiliary goal lists, e.g.\n    27→`EXTRA_GOALS`.  Each conjecture is a Python lambda on the free variables\n    28→`a, b, c` built with `+`, `*`, integer literals and no other operations.\n    29→\"\"\"\n    30→"